    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:comment "RO-Crate Workflow-Run CreateAction; GMEOW Execution is the event that enacts a procedure."
|} .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Workflow-engine surfaces — Airflow / CWL / WDL / Temporal / Nextflow.        #
#                                                                              #
# These engines publish no canonical RDF ontologies with stable term IRIs, so  #
# each alignment is a BY-REFERENCE bridge (logic:BridgeView, Principle 5):     #
# skos:relatedMatch to an informal concept IRI (a full IRI, not a registered   #
# CURIE), NOT an equivalence. As lowerings of the canonical logic:Plan process #
# model they are commitment-shifting and lossy — preservation polarity         #
# validation-only, never exact. The recurring drops the engine surfaces impose #
# on the canonical model: a logic:Iteration loop is unrolled or rejected (most #
# DAG engines forbid cycles), a logic:ConcurrentComposition is serialized where #
# the engine has no parallel gateway, and a per-outcome logic:compensation is  #
# omitted where the engine has no compensation primitive. Each such drop is    #
# stated as a STRUCTURED gmeow:lossyDrop on the bridge below (not only prose),  #
# which the mappings stage folds into the per-correspondence residue ledger in #
# generated/logic/projection-report.                                          #
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://airflow.apache.org/concept/DAG> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Apache Airflow DAG (by reference, no canonical RDF): a procedure is a DAG of tasks. Lossy lowering — Airflow forbids cycles (a logic:Iteration loop must unroll or error) and has no per-outcome compensation (omitted)." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "logic:Iteration loop: unrolls or errors (an Airflow DAG forbids cycles)" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted (Airflow has no compensation primitive)"
|} .

logic:ActionSchema skos:relatedMatch <https://airflow.apache.org/concept/Task> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Apache Airflow Task (by reference): a procedure step is an Airflow task node in the DAG."
|} .

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://w3id.org/cwl/cwl#Workflow> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Common Workflow Language Workflow (by reference, no stable RDF term IRIs): a procedure is a CWL workflow. Lossy — CWL is acyclic dataflow (a logic:Iteration loop must unroll) and carries no compensation (omitted)." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "logic:Iteration loop: unrolls (CWL is acyclic dataflow)" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted (CWL has no compensation primitive)"
|} .

logic:ActionSchema skos:relatedMatch <https://w3id.org/cwl/cwl#WorkflowStep> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Common Workflow Language WorkflowStep (by reference): a procedure step is a CWL workflow step."
|} .

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://openwdl.org/concept/Workflow> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Workflow Description Language (WDL) workflow (by reference, no canonical RDF): a procedure is a WDL workflow of calls. Lossy lowering of the canonical plan." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "logic:Iteration loop: unrolls (a WDL call graph is acyclic)" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted (WDL has no compensation primitive)"
|} .

logic:ActionSchema skos:relatedMatch <https://openwdl.org/concept/Task> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Workflow Description Language (WDL) task (by reference): a procedure step is a WDL task."
|} .

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://temporal.io/concept/Workflow> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.55 ;
    gmeow:comment "Temporal Workflow (by reference, no canonical RDF): a procedure is a Temporal workflow definition. Temporal DOES express loops and compensation (saga) imperatively, so the lowering is closer for control flow but is a code surface, not a declarative spec — carried by reference only." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "logic:Iteration loop and per-outcome logic:compensation: expressible only as imperative Temporal/saga code, not a declarative spec — carried by reference, so the canonical declarative structure is not preserved"
|} .

logic:ActionSchema skos:relatedMatch <https://temporal.io/concept/Activity> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.55 ;
    gmeow:comment "Temporal Activity (by reference): a procedure step is a Temporal activity invoked by the workflow."
|} .

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://www.nextflow.io/concept/Workflow> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Nextflow workflow (by reference, no canonical RDF): a procedure is a Nextflow dataflow workflow of processes. Lossy — Nextflow concurrency is channel-implicit (a logic:ConcurrentComposition serializes in the spec view) and there is no compensation primitive (omitted)." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "logic:ConcurrentComposition: serializes (Nextflow concurrency is channel-implicit, no explicit parallel gateway)" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted (Nextflow has no compensation primitive)"
|} .

logic:ActionSchema skos:relatedMatch <https://www.nextflow.io/concept/Process> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "Nextflow process (by reference): a procedure step is a Nextflow process node consuming/producing channels."
|} .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Guard → structured-program combinator (the combinator TREE).                #
#                                                                              #
# The DAG profile minted the flow-GRAPH layer:                                #
# logic:ControlFlowEdge ⊑ logic:ControlFlowEdge,                                  #
# the binary-edge form the DAG-workflow acyclicity certifier runs Tarjan SCC  #
# over. This block adds the COMPLEMENTARY layer the flow-graph alignment did   #
# NOT carry: the correspondence from a control-flow edge's guard VALUE        #
# (gmeow:flowGuard, a gmeow:BranchConditionType) onto the canonical           #
# structured-program COMBINATOR class an interpreter walks as a program TREE  #
# (logic:Choice / logic:Iteration / logic:ConcurrentComposition /            #
# logic:Fallback). The two forms are complementary, NOT duplicates            #
# (LOGIC.md logic:ControlFlowEdge definition): the graph edge is what the     #
# certifier reads; the combinator is what an interpreter walks.               #
#                                                                              #
# These are INTERNAL structural correspondences (gmeow → logic: core, the     #
# same gmeow→gmeow idiom the deception/narrative slices already use), each a   #
# skos:relatedMatch — NOT an equivalence: a guard value is a marker on a      #
# reified edge that INDICATES which combinator the edge realizes; it is not   #
# the combinator class itself, so equivalence would overclaim. They lower     #
# through the same SSSOM/EDOAL/SPARQL pipeline and fold into the per-          #
# correspondence loss ledger (validation-only) like every other cell.         #
#                                                                              #
# switch → logic:Choice (n-ary): logic:Choice is the BINARY co-equal-operand  #
# choice combinator (logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand). An n-way switch #
# corresponds to a right-nested cascade of binary logic:Choice nodes, so the  #
# single canonical target is logic:Choice; the n-ary nesting is the lossy     #
# drop recorded on the cell (the flat switch arity is not preserved by the    #
# binary combinator). The implicit fallback / else arm of an if or a switch   #
# corresponds to logic:Fallback (try the guarded arm, else the default arm);  #
# it is recorded as the residue note on those two cells rather than as a      #
# separate guard value, because the procedures vocabulary has no distinct     #
# "else" guard — the default arm is the un-guarded ControlFlow edge out of    #
# the branch step.                                                            #
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

gmeow:branchConditionIf skos:relatedMatch logic:Choice {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:comment "An if-then guard on a logic:ControlFlowEdge edge realizes the canonical binary choice combinator logic:Choice (the guarded then-arm vs. the alternative). Structural, not equivalent: the guard VALUE marks which combinator the reified edge realizes, it is not the combinator class. The implicit else / default arm corresponds to logic:Fallback (try the guarded arm, else the default)." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "implicit else/default arm → logic:Fallback: the default branch is the un-guarded ControlFlow edge out of the branch step, not carried as a distinct guard value"
|} .

gmeow:branchConditionLoop skos:relatedMatch logic:Iteration {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:comment "A loop-back guard on a logic:ControlFlowEdge edge realizes the canonical iteration combinator logic:Iteration (logic:iterationBody gated by logic:iterationCondition). Structural, not equivalent. A loop is a back-edge in the flow graph, so a procedure carrying a loop guard is outside the acyclic DAG fragment the certifier accepts." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "loop body / loop condition split (logic:iterationBody, logic:iterationCondition) is not carried by the flat guard value; the back-edge places the procedure outside the DAG fragment"
|} .

gmeow:branchConditionParallel skos:relatedMatch logic:ConcurrentComposition {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:comment "A parallel split/join guard on a logic:ControlFlowEdge edge realizes the canonical concurrent-composition combinator logic:ConcurrentComposition (two co-equal legs run concurrently). Structural, not equivalent." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "the conflict-serializability surface of a concurrent run (logic:ConcurrentHistory, logic:serializabilityCriterion) is derived by the native evaluator, not carried by the flat parallel guard value"
|} .

gmeow:branchConditionSwitch skos:relatedMatch logic:Choice {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.6 ;
    gmeow:comment "An n-way switch guard on a logic:ControlFlowEdge edge realizes the canonical choice combinator logic:Choice. logic:Choice is BINARY (logic:leftOperand / logic:rightOperand), so an n-way switch corresponds to a right-nested cascade of binary logic:Choice nodes; the single canonical combinator target is logic:Choice. Structural, not equivalent. The implicit default case corresponds to logic:Fallback." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "implicit default case → logic:Fallback: the default arm is the un-guarded ControlFlow edge out of the branch step, not carried as a distinct guard value" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "n-ary switch arity → right-nested binary logic:Choice cascade: the flat switch arity is not preserved by the binary combinator"
|} .

# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# openEHR Task Planning (PROC) — a HIGHER-fidelity by-reference bridge.        #
#                                                                              #
# openEHR PROC publishes no canonical RDF ontology with stable term IRIs, so   #
# each alignment is a BY-REFERENCE bridge (logic:BridgeView, Principle 5):     #
# skos:relatedMatch to a spec-anchored concept IRI, NOT an equivalence. Unlike #
# the acyclic workflow engines above, openEHR TP-VML/DLM natively expresses    #
# BOTH loops and guarded branching on real conditions, so — for a logic:Plan   #
# carrying a logic:Iteration or a logic:Choice — this lowering is faithful     #
# where the DAG engines must unroll or reject. It under-approximates only where #
# TP-VML lacks logic:'s explicit concurrency-serializability guarantee and its  #
# per-outcome logic:compensation. GMEOW moreover SUBSUMES the distinctive DLM   #
# constructs natively rather than merely bridging them: DLM `currency`          #
# (max datum age) is logic:FreshnessGuard's logic:freshnessHorizon axis and DLM #
# `time_window` (an explicit named valid-time interval) is its orthogonal       #
# logic:freshnessWindow axis; manual-notification /                             #
# callback-driven completion is logic:NotificationWaitSchema; the Instruction-  #
# State-Machine plan→execution linkage is the logic:instantiatesSchema +        #
# logic:instantiatesPlan in-band witness. Each residual drop is a STRUCTURED    #
# gmeow:lossyDrop the mappings stage folds into the per-correspondence residue  #
# ledger in generated/logic/projection-report.                                #
# --------------------------------------------------------------------------- #

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#WORK_PLAN> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:comment "openEHR Task Planning WORK_PLAN (by reference, no canonical RDF): a top-level procedure is an openEHR work plan. Higher fidelity than the acyclic engines — TP-VML/DLM carries loops and guarded branching, so a logic:Iteration or logic:Choice in the plan projects faithfully rather than unrolling. Lossy only where TP-VML lacks logic:'s concurrency-serializability and per-outcome compensation." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "logic:ConcurrentComposition: under-approximated where TP-VML has no explicit concurrency-serializability guarantee (logic:ConcurrentHistory / logic:serializabilityCriterion are derived natively, not carried)" ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted where TP-VML has no compensation primitive on a task outcome"
|} .

logic:Plan skos:relatedMatch <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#TASK_PLAN> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.65 ;
    gmeow:comment "openEHR Task Planning TASK_PLAN / SUB_PLAN (by reference): a constituent sub-procedure (gmeow:hasSubProcedure) is an openEHR task plan nested under a work plan. The sub-plan nesting round-trips; the same concurrency / compensation drops as the work-plan bridge apply." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "per-outcome logic:compensation: omitted where TP-VML has no compensation primitive on a task outcome"
|} .

logic:ActionSchema skos:relatedMatch <https://specifications.openehr.org/releases/PROC/latest/task_planning.html#TASK> {|
    gmeow:sssomFile "gmeow-work-orchestration.sssom.tsv" ;
    gmeow:justification semapv:ManualMappingCuration ;
    gmeow:confidence 0.7 ;
    gmeow:comment "openEHR Task Planning TASK / TASK_ACTION (by reference): a procedure step is an openEHR task. A DLM-gated task maps to a guarded logic:Choice step (preserved, not unrolled); a manual-notification task maps to logic:NotificationWaitSchema (subsumed natively); a DLM currency-guarded task input maps to logic:FreshnessGuard (subsumed natively) — BOTH its axes: `currency` (max age) to logic:freshnessHorizon and `time_window` (an explicit valid-time interval) to logic:freshnessWindow / logic:freshnessWindowStart / logic:freshnessWindowEnd." ;
    gmeow:lossyDrop "TP-VML task scheduling annotations (planned time / wait windows) are not carried by a bare logic:ActionSchema; scheduling is a solver-layer concern (Principle 12)"
|} .
